*.local

# .env IS tracked on purpose. Vite inlines every VITE_* var into the client
# bundle at build time, so the Firebase web config is public no matter what —
# the real access boundary is the UID allowlist in firestore.rules. Keeping it
# in the repo is what lets CI build and deploy without extra secret wiring.
# Anything genuinely secret (service accounts, API keys with write scope) must
# go in GitHub Actions secrets, never here.
.env.local
.env.*.local

